# library_books.dialogue — browsing the two library bookshelf stands.
# reached from Use on the shelves (unusables.dialogue imports this file).
# each row of a stand is one topic; each book opens one page via BookReader (data/library_books.gd).
# reading the heredity book sets dna_dates_found (the keypad follow-up stops pointing at Julian's lead).

~ left_stand
What do you want to look through?
- Scientific History
	=> left_history
- Genetics and Molecular Biology
	=> left_genetics
- Chemistry
	=> left_chemistry
- Statistics and Mathematics
	=> left_stats
- Nothing. Never mind. [Leave]
	=> END

~ left_history
Which book?
- Threads of Inheritance: A History of Heredity
	do BookReader.open("history_of_heredity")
	do Flags.set_level_flag("dna_dates_found", true)
	=> left_history
- The Voyage of the Beagle (Darwin)
	do BookReader.open("darwin_beagle")
	=> left_history
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> left_stand

~ left_genetics
Which book?
- The Physical Basis of Heredity (T. H. Morgan)
	do BookReader.open("morgan_heredity")
	=> left_genetics
- Safety Guidelines for Overworked Grad Students
	do BookReader.open("grad_safety_guidelines")
	=> left_genetics
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> left_stand

~ left_chemistry
Which book?
- The Chemical History of a Candle (Faraday)
	do BookReader.open("faraday_candle")
	=> left_chemistry
- Ignition! (John D. Clark)
	do BookReader.open("ignition")
	=> left_chemistry
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> left_stand

~ left_stats
Which book?
- The Power of Placebos (Howick)
	do BookReader.open("power_of_placebos")
	=> left_stats
- The Grammar of Science (Pearson)
	do BookReader.open("pearson_grammar")
	=> left_stats
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> left_stand

~ right_stand
What do you want to look through?
- Literature and Classics
	=> right_literature
- Philosophy
	=> right_philosophy
- Art and Architecture
	=> right_art
- University History
	=> right_history
- Nothing. Never mind. [Leave]
	=> END

~ right_literature
Which book?
- The Odyssey (Homer)
	do BookReader.open("homer_odyssey")
	=> right_literature
- Frankenstein (Mary Shelley)
	do BookReader.open("shelley_frankenstein")
	=> right_literature
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> right_stand

~ right_philosophy
Which book?
- The Republic (Plato)
	do BookReader.open("plato_republic")
	=> right_philosophy
- Utilitarianism (J. S. Mill)
	do BookReader.open("mill_utilitarianism")
	=> right_philosophy
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> right_stand

~ right_art
Which book?
- The Artist's Reality (Rothko)
	do BookReader.open("the_artists_reality")
	=> right_art
- The Poetics of Space (Bachelard)
	do BookReader.open("poetics_of_space")
	=> right_art
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> right_stand

~ right_history
Which book?
- A History of Greendale University
	do BookReader.open("greendale_history")
	=> right_history
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> right_stand

~ greene_shelf
Which book?
- Barbara La Marr: A Life in Silent Film
	do BookReader.open("la_marr_biography")
	do Flags.set_level_flag("la_marr_book_read", true)
	=> greene_shelf
- She Has Her Mother's Laugh
	do BookReader.open("she_has_her_mothers_laugh")
	=> greene_shelf
- Nothing. Never mind. [Leave]
	=> END
